---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const user = Astro.locals.user;
---
<BaseLayout user={user} seo={{ title: 'Privacy Policy — CrossLinkd', description: 'How CrossLinkd collects, uses, and protects your data.', path: '/privacy' }}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm" style="color:var(--text-mute)">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--text-soft)">
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">What we collect:</strong> account details, listing content you submit, reviews, claim information you choose to send, and basic analytics (page views, search terms in aggregate). Location is used only when you opt into “near me.”</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">What we never do:</strong> sell your personal data, or use your faith affiliation for third-party advertising. Claim notes you mark private are not published as a verification result.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">Your controls:</strong> signed-in users can <a href="/account" class="underline">download a JSON copy</a> of the profile and owned listings the database can return, or mark the account deleted. Deletion sets a deleted date and deletes matching rows in the sessions table. It does not automatically unpublish listings, and a browser can still look signed in until you sign out. Owners can remove their own listings from the dashboard. There is no notification or saved-search settings page. If you are not signed in, use the <a href="/contact" class="underline">contact form</a>. That request is saved for a person to read. It is not an instant export.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">Security:</strong> production pages are served over HTTPS. Passwords are stored as hashes, not as plain text. What you can open depends on the signed-in role. This app does not keep a separate audit log of sensitive actions. Contact, claim, and listing forms are rate-limited.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">Cookies:</strong> strictly-necessary session cookies, theme preference, and (optional) privacy-respecting analytics.</p>
      <p>Privacy questions go through the <a href="/contact" class="underline">contact page</a>. A saved message is not a promise of a reply time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
